   # Layers----------------Packet Data Unit             
P = Physical-------------------------------------Bits

D = Data Link-------------------------------------Frame

N = Network-------------------------------------Packet

T = Transport-------------------------------------Segment

S = Session-------------------------------------Data

P = Presentation-------------------------------------Data

A = Application-------------------------------------Data

* # Application layer
Appplication layer is resposible to providing an interface for the user to interact with application services or network services.
* Ex-Web browser (HTTP), Telnet

* # Presentation layer
Presentation layer is responsible to defining a standard formate to a Data.This layer needs to "reformate" the data.So, both computers agree on the same characterstics.
*  # Major function are works on this layer:-
     * Encoding-decoding
     *  Encryption-decryption
     * For example:-AVI-(video), WAV-(voice), JPEG (graphite), ASCII (text)
# Session layer
Session layer is resposible to establish, manage and terminate the sessions between the two hosts.Like when we are using any websites. wea re not only the user at that web server then this web server needs to keep track of all the different “sessions.”

*  EX:-Remote procedural call, Apple talk session protocol

# Transport layer
Transport layer is also known as heart of OSI. it is resposible to provide data mechanism. This layer is also resposible for Multiplexing-De-multiplexing 
Segmentation-Fregmentation, Error correction, flow control

* TCP and UDP are the Protocols which take care of data transport.
